    "30-implementation-1": {
      "id": "30-implementation-1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The skill's Python helpers create a Markdown bundle and check goal length. They use the Python standard library and do not execute the objective, schedule work, or manage checkpoints."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "30-implementation-2": {
      "id": "30-implementation-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Their behavior supports the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Objective Bundle and Lifecycle",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "10-system-design"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " contract. The source is under .codex/skills/setup-objective/scripts/."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "30-implementation-3": {
      "id": "30-implementation-3",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Scaffold"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "30-implementation-4": {
      "id": "30-implementation-4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The implementation is "
        },
        {
          "insert": ".codex/skills/setup-objective/scripts/create_objective.py",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true,
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": ".codex/skills/setup-objective/scripts/create_objective.py"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". It normalizes the name to a lowercase hyphenated slug and writes the goal, state, README, and five context templates."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "30-implementation-5": {
      "id": "30-implementation-5",
      "type": "structured-table",
      "props": {
        "columns": [
          "Argument",
          "Behavior"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "name",
            "Required objective name or slug."
          ],
          [
            "--title TEXT",
            "Readable title; otherwise derived from the slug."
          ],
          [
            "--root PATH",
            "Output root; defaults to objectives relative to the current directory."
          ],
          [
            "--no-examples",
            "Skip examples/.gitkeep."
          ],
          [
            "--date TEXT",
            "Initial state date; defaults to today's date. Use YYYY-MM-DD."
          ],
          [
            "--force",
            "Overwrite existing scaffold files. This replaces content, so inspect the destination first."
          ]
        ]
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "30-implementation-6": {
      "id": "30-implementation-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Overwrite refusal is per file, not a transaction across the entire bundle. A partially populated destination can receive earlier files before a later existing file causes failure. Inspect the directory after a failure instead of rerunning with --force."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "30-implementation-7": {
      "id": "30-implementation-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The templates are intentionally incomplete. A successful scaffold command means the files exist, not that the objective is ready to execute."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "30-implementation-8": {
      "id": "30-implementation-8",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Goal-Length Validator"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "30-implementation-9": {
      "id": "30-implementation-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The implementation is "
        },
        {
          "insert": ".codex/skills/setup-objective/scripts/validate_goal_length.py",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true,
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": ".codex/skills/setup-objective/scripts/validate_goal_length.py"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". It reads a file or stdin, strips surrounding whitespace and an outer fenced block, removes a leading /goal command when followed by whitespace, and counts Python string characters."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "30-implementation-10": {
      "id": "30-implementation-10",
      "type": "structured-table",
      "props": {
        "columns": [
          "Argument",
          "Behavior"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "path",
            "Optional file. When omitted, read stdin."
          ],
          [
            "--max-chars N",
            "Hard maximum; default 3,999."
          ],
          [
            "--target-chars N",
            "Optional advisory target; no target by default."
          ],
          [
            "--compact-target",
            "Use the 1,600-character advisory target unless an explicit target is set."
          ],
          [
            "--strict-target",
            "Fail above the selected target; default target becomes 1,600 if none was chosen."
          ]
        ]
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "30-implementation-11": {
      "id": "30-implementation-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The helper prints objective_chars, target_chars, and max_chars. It returns exit code 1 above the hard maximum, or above a strict target. An advisory target warning alone returns success. An empty goal can pass this length check, so semantic review remains necessary."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "30-implementation-12": {
      "id": "30-implementation-12",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The default maximum reflects the Codex TUI constraint recorded by this skill. This guide documents the local helper's behavior; it does not establish a current limit for every Codex client or other agent host."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "30-implementation-13": {
      "id": "30-implementation-13",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Implementation Choices"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "30-implementation-14": {
      "id": "30-implementation-14",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Markdown keeps objective state inspectable with ordinary repository tools. Pseudo-XML marks sections without introducing a runtime parser. The helper scripts remain small because execution belongs to the project's agent and runners."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "30-implementation-15": {
      "id": "30-implementation-15",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A project-specific runner must implement compatibility checks, atomic checkpoints, and controls itself. Documentation of a flag such as --resume does not prove that every historical AutoHDR runner meets the later guidance."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "30-implementation-16": {
      "id": "30-implementation-16",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Skill Metadata"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "30-implementation-17": {
      "id": "30-implementation-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The Codex display name and default skill prompt are in "
        },
        {
          "insert": ".codex/skills/setup-objective/agents/openai.yaml",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true,
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": ".codex/skills/setup-objective/agents/openai.yaml"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". The repository's .codex/config.toml is workspace configuration, not a portable installation requirement. Copying the skill does not require copying that configuration."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    }
  }
}
